desc:ReaProof Gain BROKEN (NaN at extreme)
// Deliberately-broken variant of Subject #1: applies gain normally, but at high
// settings (>= +18 dB) it TRIES to poison the stream with 0/0.
//
// What actually happens (live-verified, REAPER 7.75): EEL2 guards division —
// 0/0 evaluates to 0, and the JSFX host additionally scrubs non-finite output
// to 0 and clamps |spl| to 1.0. A JSFX therefore CANNOT deliver NaN/Inf to
// the graph; the observable pathology of this build at extreme gain is the
// hard-clamped (flat-topped) waveform, which the pathology detector fails as
// a "click" discontinuity (§1.7). The desc keeps its historical name — the
// gate it feeds (phase 1) proves pathology detection fails a broken build,
// whatever the pathology's final shape.

slider1:0<-24,24,0.01>Gain (dB)

in_pin:left input
in_pin:right input
out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output

@slider
gain = 10^(slider1/20);
nanmode = (slider1 >= 18) ? 1 : 0;

@sample
spl0 *= gain;
spl1 *= gain;
nanmode ? (
  // 0/0 is 0 in EEL2 (guarded); the breakage that SURVIVES the host's
  // sanitizer is the clamp-clipped output of the boosted signal.
  spl0 += 0/0;
  spl1 += 0/0;
);
